==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Haniwanwan]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 50~56.67 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,700f</sup>.
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Ragin' Gory]] spawns after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Great Ape Luza]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**4 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.
**1 [[Loris]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
**1 [[Casaurian Darkjo]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage debuts the Uncanny Legend: Great Ape Luza. Luza as an enemy is a standard Relic backliner with a high TBA, but hits very hard. Notably, Luza's attack is actually two hits very close together. Also notably, Luza is both a Relic and Behemoth enemy, meaning if you get your UL Mythic True Forms he gets jumped very efficiently. Most notably, getting [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Naala]]'s True Form, Awakened Naala, gives her gargantuan stats against Luza.

At the start, use the slow startoff to stall for cash, which shouldn't be too hard to do. On base hit, you're met by Luza and Loris, and after a bit Darkjo is added to the fray. This looks pretty terrifying, but you can use the power of [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] to Freeze Luza and rack up ridiculous amounts of damage onto him before Darkjo arrives. Once Darkjo does come out, Luza's most likely on very low health, meaning you can use a second Doron as well as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] to finish him off.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]]: Combined with Doron, Idi allows you to rack up very high damage against Luza very quickly.
*Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]: C.A.T's extremely good mobility and high damage against Darks makes him a very strong unit for the Darkjo.
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]]: Similar to Idi, you can spam a bunch of Guards and then beat up Luza extremely fast combined with Doron.
*[[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]]: If you have Egg Pod at this point, you basically win instantly. Egg Pod has extremely high damage against Behemoths and is practically immortal against them given his 50% Dodge chance.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: A strong counter for the Ragin' Gories.

==Trivia==
*The enemy base is similar to that of the [[Empire of Cats]] [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]] stage.
*This stage reuses music from the [[Moon (Into the Future)|Moon]] stage of [[Into the Future]].
*This is one of the only stages in the game to have a chance of rewarding a [[Battle Items#Treasure Radar|Treasure Radar]], the others being [[Villains Jungle]], [[Unkept Promises]], [[An Ancient Curse]], [[Aku Altar's Seal]], [[Ape Lord's Revenge]] and [[Birth of True Man]].

